From cc7a988069ab9e0405eb28de1ce541f6256cd134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skywalker512 <houzhenhong@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:42:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] configure: Don't use the preloader on Android.

Apps targeting Android 10 (API 29) or later cannot execve() files in their
data directory (SELinux W^X), which is where an app keeps Wine. They run
such programs through the system dynamic linker instead
(/system/bin/linker64 prog args...), and the linker cannot load the static
preloader. On 64-bit hosts ntdll already reserves the preloader's address
ranges itself when there is no preloader (mmap_init).

Amphora-Origin: new (targetSdk 36, 2026-11-08)
Amphora-Upstream: android-only
---
 configure.ac | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 5376e11f353..f1d39a7896d 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -2140,6 +2140,12 @@ dnl **** Platform-specific checks ****
 AC_SUBST(WINELOADER_PROGRAMS,"wine")
 
 case $host_os in
+  linux-android*)
+    dnl Apps targeting Android 10 (API 29) or later cannot execve() files in their
+    dnl data directory, so they run them through the system dynamic linker, which
+    dnl cannot load the static preloader. On 64-bit, ntdll reserves the same areas
+    dnl at startup when there is no preloader (mmap_init).
+    ;;
   linux*)
     if test $HOST_ARCH != unknown
     then
